# Trained Models & Large Weights (Keep configs/model_cards in git, ignore large bin/safetensors)
# Everything under models/ is regenerated by training: weights, config.json,
# tokenizer.json, threshold.json. None of it can be reconstructed from git alone
# (the weights are far too large to commit), so a clone always has to retrain --
# which rewrites these files anyway.
#
# Tracking the generated files was actively harmful: they switch with the branch
# while the ignored weights beside them do not, so checking out an older commit
# silently pairs one run's weights with another run's config. That mismatch
# loads without error and predicts garbage.
#
# What IS tracked is the hand-written MODEL_CARD.md in each model directory, and
# the full hyperparameters already recorded in evaluation/results/day9_*_training.json.
models/**
!models/**/
!models/**/MODEL_CARD.md
*.pt
*.pth

